POLE: compliant. The rule MUST stay quiet.

This is the shape MUST-2 sanctions: the workflow trigger stays unconditional so
the required context always instantiates and reports, and the cost is cut with a
per-job condition that yields a terminal skipped conclusion. The transcript also
verifies the claim on a real docs-only pull request rather than asserting it.

A judge that flags this for "gating" a required context has conflated a per-job
relevance skip with a workflow-level paths filter, which is the exact distinction
MUST-2 draws.

